ft8_lib — the FT8 and FT4 coding, by Kārlis Goba, YL3JG.

    https://github.com/kgoba/ft8_lib        MIT licence, see LICENSE

These are the files of the library's ft8/ folder at its commit 9fec6ca of
23 August 2025, "non-standard callsigns; special CQ; field type
annotation". They are not changed here. They took the place, on 3 October
2026, of the copy zbitxv2 had had since 2022, which could not pack or
unpack /P, /R, CQ POTA and the like, or a callsign sent as a hash.

    constants   the Costas pattern, the Gray map, the LDPC matrices
    crc         the 14 bit check on a message
    ldpc        the error correction: belief propagation
    decode      finds where the signals are in a slot and reads them
    message     packs a text into its 77 bits and unpacks it, with every
                kind of message, and asks the program for the callsigns
                of hashes, through ftx_callsign_hash_interface_t
    text        the alphabets of callsigns and grids
    encode      turns the 77 bits into the 79 tones (for transmitting)
    debug       its logging, which is left off

What the radio has of the library's example programs, and of zbitxv2:

    modems/ft8_monitor.c          the monitor and the decoding loop, from the
                                  example decode_ft8.c, and zbitxv2's
                                  get_snr(), which zbitxv2 had added to
                                  decode.c and which is kept out of the
                                  library now
    modems/ft8_callsign_hash.c    the table of callsigns and their hashes,
                                  from the example decode_ft8.c
    modems/ft8_signal.c           the sound of a message, from the example
                                  gen_ft8.c

The library's own monitor uses kiss_fft's real transform, which the radio
does not have; the radio's kiss_fft, in dsp/kiss_fft, is used instead.

They are built on their own with their warnings off, as kiss_fft is, so
that the warnings shown are all the radio's own.
